    "q-140761": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140761",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{750}^{∘}$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?",
      "worked_solution": "We wish to express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{750}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta ={750}^{∘}.$\n\nFirst, we find an angle that's coterminal with ${750}^{∘}$ that lies in the range $[0,{360}^{∘}).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get our desired angle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{750}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} & ={390}^{∘} \\\\ {750}^{∘}-2\\cdot {360}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our coterminal angle is acute and lies in the first quadrant. Therefore, ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘},$ and we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{750}^{∘}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253971/assets/33a1982c3b7aea8455770d354494895a19e14a5f9d4b3fa03ffeb5ef9ba32697.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140761-a",
