    "q-140776": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140776",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?",
      "worked_solution": "We wish to express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta ={480}^{∘}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get our desired angle.\n\n$$\n{480}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}={120}^{∘}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253971/assets/edbfa5b5fd12661d72de833198c5621012cd9e6ecc6b93111c536b578622b4e4.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta ={120}^{∘}$ is in the $2$nd quadrant, the reference angle is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}={180}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The sine function is positive $(+)$ in the second quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}=+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{480}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
